&lt;h4 id=&#34;-advanced-features&#34;&gt;⚠️ Advanced features
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;For some advanced features (ex: Export as PDF) Docs relies on XL packages from BlockNote. These are licenced under GPL and are not MIT compatible. You can perfectly use Docs without these packages by setting the environment variable &lt;code&gt;PUBLISH_AS_MIT&lt;/code&gt; to true. That way you&amp;rsquo;ll build an image of the application without the features that are not MIT compatible. Read the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://producthunt.programnotes.cn/docs/env.md&#34; &gt;environment variables documentation&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;getting-started-&#34;&gt;Getting started 🔧
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;test-it&#34;&gt;Test it
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can test Docs on your browser by visiting this &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://impress-preprod.beta.numerique.gouv.fr/docs/6ee5aac4-4fb9-457d-95bf-bb56c2467713/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;demo document&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;run-docs-locally&#34;&gt;Run Docs locally
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚠️ The methods described below for running Docs locally is &lt;strong&gt;for testing purposes only&lt;/strong&gt;. It is based on building Docs using &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://min.io/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Minio&lt;/a&gt; as an S3-compatible storage solution. Of course you can choose any S3-compatible storage solution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prerequisite&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Make sure you have a recent version of Docker and &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://docs.docker.com/compose/install&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Docker Compose&lt;/a&gt; installed on your laptop, then type:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ docker -v
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;Docker version 20.10.2, build 2291f61
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ docker compose version
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;Docker Compose version v2.32.4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚠️ You may need to run the following commands with &lt;code&gt;sudo&lt;/code&gt;, but this can be avoided by adding your user to the local &lt;code&gt;docker&lt;/code&gt; group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project bootstrap&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to start working on the project is to use &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.gnu.org/software/make/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;GNU Make&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ make bootstrap FLUSH_ARGS=&amp;#39;--no-input&amp;#39;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This command builds the &lt;code&gt;app-dev&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;frontend-dev&lt;/code&gt; containers, installs dependencies, performs database migrations and compiles translations. It&amp;rsquo;s a good idea to use this command each time you are pulling code from the project repository to avoid dependency-related or migration-related issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your Docker services should now be up and running 🎉&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can access the project by going to &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://localhost:3000&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;http://localhost:3000&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be prompted to log in. The default credentials are:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;username: impress
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;password: impress
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;📝 Note that if you need to run them afterwards, you can use the eponymous Make rule:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ make run
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;⚠️ For the frontend developer, it is often better to run the frontend in development mode locally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To do so, install the frontend dependencies with the following command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ make frontend-development-install
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;And run the frontend locally in development mode with the following command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ make run-frontend-development
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;To start all the services, except the frontend container, you can use the following command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ make run-backend
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;To execute frontend tests &amp;amp; linting only&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ make frontend-test
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ make frontend-lint
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adding content&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can create a basic demo site by running this command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ make demo
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Finally, you can check all available Make rules using this command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ make help
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Django admin&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can access the Django admin site at:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://localhost:8071/admin&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;http://localhost:8071/admin&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You first need to create a superuser account:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-fallback&#34; data-lang=&#34;fallback&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;$ make superuser
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;feedback-&#34;&gt;Feedback 🙋‍♂️🙋‍♀️
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;We&amp;rsquo;d love to hear your thoughts, and hear about your experiments, so come and say hi on &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://matrix.to/#/#docs-official:matrix.org&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Matrix&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;roadmap-&#34;&gt;Roadmap 💡
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Want to know where the project is headed? &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/orgs/numerique-gouv/projects/13/views/11&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;🗺️ Checkout our roadmap&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;license-&#34;&gt;License 📝
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This work is released under the MIT License (see &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/suitenumerique/docs/blob/main/LICENSE&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;LICENSE&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While Docs is a public-driven initiative, our license choice is an invitation for private sector actors to use, sell and contribute to the project.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;contributing-&#34;&gt;Contributing 🙌
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;This project is intended to be community-driven, so please, do not hesitate to &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://matrix.to/#/#docs-official:matrix.org&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;get in touch&lt;/a&gt; if you have any question related to our implementation or design decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can help us with translations on &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://crowdin.com/project/lasuite-docs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Crowdin&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you intend to make pull requests, see &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/suitenumerique/docs/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;CONTRIBUTING&lt;/a&gt; for guidelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;directory-structure&#34;&gt;Directory structure:
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;9
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-markdown&#34; data-lang=&#34;markdown&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;docs
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;├── bin - executable scripts or binaries that are used for various tasks, such as setup scripts, utility scripts, or custom commands.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;├── crowdin - for crowdin translations, a tool or service that helps manage translations for the project.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;├── docker - Dockerfiles and related configuration files used to build Docker images for the project. These images can be used for development, testing, or production environments.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;├── docs - documentation for the project, including user guides, API documentation, and other helpful resources.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;├── env.d/development - environment-specific configuration files for the development environment. These files might include environment variables, configuration settings, or other setup files needed for development.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;├── gitlint - configuration files for &lt;span class=&#34;sb&#34;&gt;`gitlint`&lt;/span&gt;, a tool that enforces commit message guidelines to ensure consistency and quality in commit messages.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;├── playground - experimental or temporary code, where developers can test new features or ideas without affecting the main codebase.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;└── src - main source code directory, containing the core application code, libraries, and modules of the project.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;credits-&#34;&gt;Credits ❤️
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;stack&#34;&gt;Stack
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Docs is built on top of &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.django-rest-framework.org/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Django Rest Framework&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://nextjs.org/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Next.js&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.blocknotejs.org/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;BlockNote.js&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://tiptap.dev/docs/hocuspocus/introduction&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;HocusPocus&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://yjs.dev/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Yjs&lt;/a&gt;. We thank the contributors of all these projects for their awesome work!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud sponsors of &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.blocknotejs.org/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;BlockNotejs&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://yjs.dev/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Yjs&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;gov--open-source&#34;&gt;Gov ❤️ open source
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Docs is the result of a joint effort led by the French 🇫🇷🥖 (&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.numerique.gouv.fr/dinum/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;DINUM&lt;/a&gt;) and German 🇩🇪🥨 governments (&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://zendis.de/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;ZenDiS&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are always looking for new public partners (we are currently onboarding the Netherlands 🇳🇱🧀), feel free to &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;mailto:docs@numerique.gouv.fr&#34; &gt;reach out&lt;/a&gt; if you are interested in using or contributing to Docs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p align=&#34;center&#34;&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
